    "As the evaluation methodologist, I agree and would emphasize reachability honesty. A status indicator that degrades gracefully when the lab moves, paired with a configurable location and on-demand re-probing, prevents the bridge from presenting stale or misleading state as fact. The concept bridge that maps lab mechanisms onto catalog records adds value without pretending to transfer live results. I would rather see honest links and tables that admit distance than a brittle integration that breaks or, worse, silently shows yesterday lab as if it were today.",
