    "As the continual-learning researcher, I dissent gently by asking for just enough coupling to keep the bridge honest over time. A read-only tab can drift from the lab it describes, especially as scenarios, evolvers and bands evolve, so I would want version signals and build-time checks that mapped identifiers still exist on both sides. The goal is not execution but fidelity, ensuring that every pattern and scenario link resolves and every figure renders. A bridge that cannot silently disagree with its lab is what lets two books share mechanisms without sharing runtime risk."
