    "As the continual-learning researcher, I agree and would sharpen the scope of what comparative evidence can guide. Knowing that scoped learning preserves earlier families while global rewriting leaks across them is actionable architectural knowledge, even though it says nothing about the next unseen domain. The streams are rehearsals with known choreography, valuable because they make forgetting observable under controlled drift rather than leaving it to be discovered in production. I would use sweeps to select mechanisms and orderings to fear, then verify those selections elsewhere before claiming readiness.",
